A||||4||Ed||Sacramento Club News||||10||
Z||000000||Ed||04-02-2000||08:10 PM||||Well, I volunteered to be President of the Northern California Chapter of the FOCOA. Our area of interest is around Sacramento, California. <P>I'm going to try to stir up new interest in this local club, and I'm inviting YOU.  <P>We're going for a Sierra foothills wine country tour next Sunday, April 16. <P>Any Sacramento locals to this board give me an e-mail if you would like to participate in this drive or are interested in joining up. <P>And for you going to the Fiero Fest in San Diego, at least two of us are going down from this area.  ||||reg||10
Z||000001||fieroshop||04-02-2000||08:15 PM||||Ed, I need you to e-mail me your address so that I can send you the newsletter from Golden Gate Fieros. I am the membership/newsletter editor/historian. Also check out our new site at <A HREF="http://www.goldengatefieros.org" TARGET=_blank>http://www.goldengatefieros.org</A> <BR>There will several of our group going to San Diego.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||terryk||04-02-2000||10:27 PM||||Well, I'm up by Auburn so I might consider it. Wine? There's wine up here? Maybe you meant wino's or gold or something like that. I figured the weather was too brutal for wine vineyards.||||reg||12
Z||000003||Big O||04-03-2000||01:31 AM||||Good to hear there is some activity going to get a club started here in the Central Valley.  I'm located in Manteca and will try to make some of the outings and meetings if possible.  I work six days a week and we don't get out of the store until 6-6:30 in the evenings. but I do have the occaisional Sunday afternoon free.  Keep me informed of your activities and where you plan to meet.||||reg||10
Z||000004||Ed||04-03-2000||09:17 PM||||OOPS!  April 9 wine tour.<P>I'll get  back to each of you separately.<P>Yes, there's wine to the south of Auburn, actually south of Placerville.  Several wineries in El Dorado and Amador counties.  I think there's some north of Auburn by Nevada City.  <P>All of the above have good Fiero drives. <P>This club actually has been around for about 15 years, but has been in decline recently.  Some of the Golden Gate Fiero members were members of Sacramento first and were inspired to start up their own club.  So, we'll see if we can revitilize this local chapter.  <P>We actually hosted a regional festival a few years ago, and have helped Reno (a little) with their two regional festivals.  So we do have a history.  <P>Maybe we can have a drive towards Modesto and meet those of you in that area.  I'm somewhat familiar with the hills to the east so I know there's some good drives available.      ||||reg||1
